Snapshots: One of NetApp's biggest strengths.
Point-in-time image of data.

Imagine a Word Document At 10 AM: Version 1
Create snapshot.

At 2 PM: Delete important content
Oops.

Restore snapshot.Back to 10 AM state.

How Snapshot Works

Not: Copy all data
Instead: Remember where data blocks are

Initially almost free.

Example:
1 TB volume.
Creating snapshot:
Time: seconds
Space: almost zero


Traditional backup:
Time: hours
Space: 1 TB

Interview Favorite:
Snapshot vs Backup

Snapshot:
Fast
Same storage system
Short-term recovery

Backup:
Separate copy
Disaster protection
Long-term retention

Filesystem State @ 10:00 AM:
Traditional Copy
1TB volume
→ 1TB storage needed

Expensive.

Snapshot Uses metadata. Stores only changed blocks.

Volume Snapshot Changed blocks only

Extremely space-efficient.

Benefits:
✅ Fast
✅ Recovery
✅ Backup
✅ Versioning

Interview Question?
Why are snapshots faster than backups?
Because snapshots don't copy all data. They mostly preserve metadata references.
